.TH "tum" "1" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
tum \[em] borrow, reuse, and flip\-flop utility panes inside tmux
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tum\f[R] \f[I]command\f[R] [\f[I]args\f[R]\&...]
.PP
\f[B]tum\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]tum\f[R] \f[I]command\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
\f[B]tum\f[R] manages \[lq]borrowed\[rq] utility panes (htop, a log
tail, an editor, a DB console, \&...)
beside your host pane in tmux.
A utility is defined once in a \f[CR].util\f[R] file;
\f[CR]tum borrow\f[R] attaches an instance beside the current pane, and
\f[CR]tum flip\f[R] hides/shows it without losing its process.
Instances are reused: hidden ones return to the same host, pool ones can
be borrowed by any host, and \f[CR]tum new\f[R] makes an instance owned
by one host.
.SS COMMANDS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum borrow\f[R] [\f[I]util\f[R]|\f[I]layout\f[R]] Attach a utility
(or layout) beside the host; reuse a hidden instance if one exists for
this host, else the pool, else create.
With no argument, open the chooser.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum new\f[R] \f[I]util\f[R] Create an instance owned by the current
host (flip returns it only here).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum flip\f[R] [\f[I]slot\f[R]] Hide/show the slot\[cq]s bound
thing.
No slot → context\-aware (focused borrowed pane, else the host\[cq]s
single thing, else chooser).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum close\f[R] Kill the focused borrowed pane (or chooser\-pick).
No confirmation.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum push\f[R] / \f[B]tum pop\f[R] Detach the focused borrowed pane
onto a LIFO stack / reattach the top.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum import\f[R] [\f[I]name\f[R]] Make the current pane a temporary
utility (anonymous), or capture it to a named \f[CR].util\f[R] file.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum ls\f[R] List every utility pane across sessions with its state.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum check\f[R] List orphans (utility whose host pane is dead).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum status\f[R] / \f[B]tum prompt\f[R] Emit status\-bar / PS1
glyphs for host, borrowed, and orphan panes.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]tum popup\f[R] / \f[B]tum cheatsheet\f[R] Open a
\f[CR]display\-popup\f[R] menu of all commands / a list of key bindings.
.SS OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R] Print a short synopsis (extracted
from this manpage\[cq]s source) for the given command, or the command
index for bare \f[B]tum\f[R].
.SS EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
tum borrow htop          # attach htop beside this pane (reuse or create)
tum new editor           # an editor owned by this host
tum flip                 # hide/show the focused borrowed thing
tum ls                   # see every utility pane and its state
.EE
.SS FILES
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[I]\[ti]/.config/tum/\f[R].util* Utility and layout definitions.
See \f[B]tum\-defs\f[R](5).
